  "scientific_limits": {
    "en": "One actual paired-valve fossil. Preserve curved free valve and attached elongated valve as Fig9. No borrowed shells or whole-species life reconstruction. Public genus-level identification retains documented species reassignment history. {\"unit\": \"meters\", \"working_dimensions_mm\": {\"height_z\": 60, \"width_x\": 50, \"depth_y\": 35}, \"basis\": \"Fig9 is labelled x1. Letter-sized scan suggests approximately 55-65mm total height and 45-55mm width. These are scan-derived rounded working dimensions, NOT direct caliper measurements. Depth35mm is inferred from oblique form.\", \"uncertainty\": \"Scan resampling/original print size uncertain; do not claim exact60mm specimen. No unseen basal extension.\"}",
    "zh": "原创低多边形研究；形态、尺度及不确定性严格以本次已核参考为界。原始限定：One actual paired-valve fossil. Preserve curved free valve and attached elongated valve as Fig9. No borrowed shells or whole-species life reconstruction. Public genus-level identification retains documented species reassignment history. {\"unit\": \"meters\", \"working_dimensions_mm\": {\"height_z\": 60, \"width_x\": 50, \"depth_y\": 35}, \"basis\": \"Fig9 is labelled x1. Letter-sized scan suggests approximately 55-65mm total height and 45-55mm width. These are scan-derived rounded working dimensions, NOT direct caliper measurements. Depth35mm is inferred from oblique form.\", \"uncertainty\": \"Scan resampling/original print size uncertain; do not claim exact60mm specimen. No unseen basal extension.\"}"
